      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start, but \"critics argue\" feels a bit vague. looking at the data, it seems like the growth and market expansion were pretty definitive, whereas the inequality thing is more of a social debate. wouldn't it be more accurate to say the primary consensus is that deregulation was the main driver of the growth seen in that era?",
